SUMMARY:Seeing Light: Landscape Photography at the North Carolina Arboretum
DESCRIPTION:Seeing Light: Landscape Photography at the North Carolina Arboretum\nwith Joseph Prater \nSaturday\, November 7  |  9 am – 12 pm \nRegister Here!\nParticipants will explore the Arboretum while learning the fundamentals of landscape photography\, including exposure\, composition\, working with natural light\, and recognizing compelling scenes. Instruction is entirely field-based and welcomes photographers of all experience levels\, including those using smartphones. \nThis program will take place outside and will follow easy trails and paved walkways. Dress for the weather and prepare to be outside for the entire program time. \nJoey Prater is a North Carolina-based landscape photographer whose work is inspired by the mountains\, forests\, and changing seasons of the Southeast. With a lifelong love of the outdoors and years spent exploring public lands\, he enjoys creating images that showcase both the beauty and character of wild places. Joey is passionate about sharing his knowledge with photographers of all experience levels\, helping others build confidence while developing their own creative vision. His goal is to inspire people to slow down\, explore with intention\, and experience a deeper connection with the landscapes around them. \n●  Members: Remember to enter your promo code upon checkout to receive your 10% member discount! Email adulteducation@ncarboretum.org with questions. \n●  See a full listing of Adult Education Programs at the North Carolina Arboretum here! Questions? Check our FAQs. \n●  We are committed to fostering a diverse\, supportive learning community. If the cost of a class is a barrier for you\, please complete this scholarship form and we will see what kind of assistance we can provide. \n●  Follow us on Facebook & Instagram! \n●  Join our Adult Education Student Hub on Discord! \n●  Interested in supporting the NC Arboretum more directly? Donate to the ONE Fund here. \nSee all of our classes open for registration here!
