SUMMARY:Handmade Holiday: Mosaic Mirror Workshop
DESCRIPTION:Handmade Holiday: Mosaic Mirror Workshop\nwith Linda Pannullo \nFriday\, December 4  |  12 – 4pm \nRegister Here!\nAll levels welcome! Learn basic mosaic techniques and create a piece of art to embellish your home. Instructor will provide 12″ substrate with an 8″ mirror. Students will decorate the 2″ border with glass\, tile and other embellishments. All materials\, tools\, adhesives\, physical handouts provided. Students may also bring jewelry\, special items to add to their mirror. \nLinda Pannullo is a local mosaic artist that uses both traditional and contemporary for my art. Her work ranges from the whimsical to fine art\, from eclectic materials to the traditional stained glass and 3D sculptures. She loves to teach and currently instructs at the John C Campbell Folk School in Brasstown\, NC\, Olive’s Porch\, the Purple Crayon and Trackside Studios in Asheville. She is very fond of FUNctional Art and love bringing new folks into the mosaic world. One of her biggest honors is to be the 1st mosaic artist to exhibit at the NC Arboretum and have a permanent mosaic installation\, Nature’s Throne there. \n●  Pre-registration is required for all classes unless otherwise detailed above. \n●  Members: Remember to enter your promo code upon checkout to receive your 10% member discount! Email adulteducation@ncarboretum.org with questions. \n●  See a full listing of Adult Education Programs at the North Carolina Arboretum here! Questions? Check our FAQs. \n●  We are committed to fostering a diverse\, supportive learning community. If the cost of a class is a barrier for you\, please complete this scholarship form and we will see what kind of assistance we can provide. \n●  Follow us on Facebook & Instagram! Or join our Adult Education Student Hub on Discord! \n●  Interested in supporting the NC Arboretum more directly? Donate to the ONE Fund here. \nSee all of our classes open for registration here!
